usage: audit_priors.py [-h] --manifest MANIFEST --output OUTPUT [--fold FOLD]
                       [--samples SAMPLES]
                       [--sampling {balanced,conventional,both}] [--seed SEED]
                       [--epoch EPOCH] [--patch-size PATCH_SIZE]
                       [--thin-radius-mm THIN_RADIUS_MM]
                       [--fov-pad-mm FOV_PAD_MM]
                       [--max-centerline-points-per-case MAX_CENTERLINE_POINTS_PER_CASE]

Read-only, deterministic ASOCA prior-label audit; numpy/scipy only, no torch.
Training cases only. Auxiliary labels stay unchanged. Image-only HU centroid
baselines use leave-one-patient-out folds inside the 32 training cases. They
are descriptive probes, not evidence that a neural classifier can learn these
labels.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --manifest MANIFEST
  --output OUTPUT
  --fold FOLD
  --samples SAMPLES     TOTAL patches; split equally if sampling=both
  --sampling {balanced,conventional,both}
  --seed SEED
  --epoch EPOCH
  --patch-size PATCH_SIZE
  --thin-radius-mm THIN_RADIUS_MM
  --fov-pad-mm FOV_PAD_MM
  --max-centerline-points-per-case MAX_CENTERLINE_POINTS_PER_CASE
